@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy Policy";
}

<div class="container py-4">
    <div class="mb-5 text-center">
        <h1 class="display-5 fw-bold">RaceDay Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="text-muted">
            Your information matters to us.
        </p>
        <span class="badge bg-primary">Last updated: 24 October 2026</span>
    </div>

    <div class="card border-0 shadow-sm mb-4">
        <div class="card-body p-4">
            <h2 class="h4 fw-bold">1. Introduction</h2>
            <p>
                RaceDay is an event management platform designed to help
                organisers manage sporting events and allow participants
                to discover events, enter competitions and view their results.
            </p>
            <p class="mb-0">
                This policy explains what information RaceDay may collect,
                why it is used and how it should be protected.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="card border-0 shadow-sm mb-4">
        <div class="card-body p-4">
            <h2 class="h4 fw-bold">2. Information We Collect</h2>
            <p>Depending on how you use RaceDay, information may include:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>Your full name and email address.</li>
                <li>Your phone number, if provided.</li>
                <li>Your account role, such as Participant or Organiser.</li>
                <li>Event entries, categories and participation status.</li>
                <li>Event results, including finishing times and positions.</li>
                <li>Profile pictures or event images, if these features are used.</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="mb-0">
                RaceDay should only collect information needed to provide
                and maintain its event management services.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="card border-0 shadow-sm mb-4">
        <div class="card-body p-4">
            <h2 class="h4 fw-bold">3. How We Use Your Information</h2>
            <p>Information may be used to:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>Create and manage user accounts.</li>
                <li>Authenticate users and apply role-based access.</li>
                <li>Display sporting events and manage enrolments.</li>
                <li>Record, manage and display event results.</li>
                <li>Allow users to view and update permitted profile details.</li>
                <li>Maintain the security and reliability of the platform.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="card border-0 shadow-sm mb-4">
        <div class="card-body p-4">
            <h2 class="h4 fw-bold">4. Passwords and Account Security</h2>
            <p>
                User passwords should be stored as secure password hashes
                rather than readable plain text. Access to account features
                should be restricted according to authentication status
                and assigned role.
            </p>
            <p class="mb-0">
                Users should keep their login credentials confidential and
                log out after using a shared device. No online system can
                guarantee absolute security.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="card border-0 shadow-sm mb-4">
        <div class="card-body p-4">
            <h2 class="h4 fw-bold">5. Sharing and Public Information</h2>
            <p>
                Information may be visible to authorised organisers when
                needed to manage events and entries. Results may be displayed
                to users where the event's publication settings permit it.
            </p>
            <p class="mb-0">
                RaceDay should not sell users' personal information. Any
                disclosure to service providers or other parties should be
                limited to what is necessary, lawful and appropriately
                protected.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="card border-0 shadow-sm mb-4">
        <div class="card-body p-4">
            <h2 class="h4 fw-bold">6. Data Storage and Retention</h2>
            <p>
                Account and event information may be stored in the platform's
                database. Images may be stored using an image-storage service
                if that feature is configured.
            </p>
            <p class="mb-0">
                Information should only be retained for as long as necessary
                for legitimate platform purposes or applicable legal
                requirements, and should be securely deleted when appropriate.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="card border-0 shadow-sm mb-4">
        <div class="card-body p-4">
            <h2 class="h4 fw-bold">7. Your Privacy Rights</h2>
            <p>
                Subject to applicable law, users may request access to their
                personal information, ask for inaccurate information to be
                corrected, or raise concerns about how their information is
                handled.
            </p>
            <p class="mb-0">
                In South Africa, the Protection of Personal Information Act
                (POPIA) may apply to the processing of personal information.
                Requests should be directed to the person or organisation
                responsible for operating RaceDay.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="card border-0 shadow-sm mb-4">
        <div class="card-body p-4">
            <h2 class="h4 fw-bold">8. Cookies and Sessions</h2>
            <p class="mb-0">
                RaceDay uses session-based functionality to support login
                status and access to account features. Session cookies help
                maintain a user's authenticated session and should be handled
                securely. Users should log out when finished, especially on
                shared devices.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="card border-0 shadow-sm mb-4">
        <div class="card-body p-4">
            <h2 class="h4 fw-bold">9. Changes to This Policy</h2>
            <p class="mb-0">
                This policy may be updated when RaceDay's features or privacy
                practices change. The latest version should be published on
                this page with an updated revision date.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="alert alert-info border-0 mt-4">
        <h2 class="h5 fw-bold">Questions or concerns?</h2>
        <p class="mb-0">
            Contact the organisation responsible for operating RaceDay
            to raise a privacy question or request concerning your
            personal information.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="text-center mt-4">
        <a asp-controller="Home"
           asp-action="Index"
           class="btn btn-primary">
            Back to RaceDay Home
        </a>
    </div>
</div>